Snapshots contain the data of a specified l_ssd volume at a particular point in time.
The data can include the Instance's operating system,
configuration information and/or files stored on the volume.

l_ssd volumes can be created from snapshots.

USAGE:
  scw instance snapshot <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  create                     Create a snapshot from a specified volume
  delete                     Delete a snapshot
  export-to-object-storage   Export a snapshot to Object Storage
  get                        Get a snapshot
  import-from-object-storage Import a snapshot from Object Storage
  list                       List snapshots
  update                     Update a snapshot

WORKFLOW COMMANDS:
  wait                       Wait for snapshot to reach a stable state

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for snapshot
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands
      --web[=true|false]                 open console page for the current resource

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw instance snapshot [command] --help" for more information about a command.
